                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1600" notBefore="1500">
                        <p>16th century?, <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName>: wood boards; brown leather, each cover blind-tooled with quadruple lines and a roll 
                           to form a central panel which contains gilt florets at the corners and a central gilt ‘yh’s’ monogram in a circle; original spine lost; two fore-edge clasps, 
                           of which the upper survives with its brown leather strap tooled with blind and gilt lines and metal-tipped (but two holes near centre of back cover suggest 
                           previous strap-and-pin fastenings); edges gilt, gauffered. Rebacked in matching leather, 20th century, Bodleian
                        </p>
                        
                     </binding>
